transip-rest (0.1.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * client.py: fix the TransIP API access token lifecycle. Every call
    used to request a new token under the same fixed label, which
    TransIP rejects with "the label ... is already used in another
    active access token" once the previous (still unexpired) token
    under that label is still active - observed during a certbot
    --dry-run. Each token request now gets a unique label
    suffix under the configured prefix (same pattern TransIP's own
    Go SDK, transip/gotransip, uses), expiry is read from the
    token's own JWT "exp" claim instead of guessed from the
    expiration_time string, and a new optional on-disk cache
    (token_cache_path, see new tokencache.py) lets a still-valid
    token survive across separate process invocations. A 401 on a
    resource call now triggers one automatic retry with a fresh
    token instead of a confusing error.

 -- Personal Builder <personal@builder.invalid>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0200

